{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395573-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-stv","id":1395573,"title":"What Would You Like to See in the STV?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-10T03:56:38-07:00","id":1395573,"title":"What Would You Like to See in the STV?","content":"So while I have worked on some future titles for the Storyteller's Vault, I have wondered if there is some preference in the community towards seeing any certain type of supplements that people would be interested in seeing. While the fun thing about the STV is that it lets you to write what you love to write, I do think that having such a discussion could be beneficial for both myself and any other potential STV writer (at the very least, it would help me to priorotize certain projects over others, and I do need to narrow my list somehow :P).<br /> <br /> So, what preferences would you have ofr a future STV material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T08:31:10-07:00","id":1395599,"title":"","content":"I apologise for immediately going off topic, but what I'd like to see is more reasonably priced products. I can't really justify buying anything on the STV because the cost for amount of content is quite a bit higher than for the official products which (I believe and hope) have higher production value and quality control. Last time I checked in was during a sale where an already discounted bundle of VtR products still had a higher price per page than official books at full price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T08:44:40-07:00","id":1395603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395573-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-stv?p=1395599#post1395599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologise for immediately going off topic, but what I'd like to see is more reasonably priced products. I can't really justify buying anything on the STV because the cost for amount of content is quite a bit higher than for the official products which (I believe and hope) have higher production value and quality control. Last time I checked in was during a sale where an already discounted bundle of VtR products still had a higher price per page than official books at full price.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is well understood. I actually tried to recalculate the &quot;value per page&quot; when I decided on the price for my title, and making sure those titles are of reasonable price is indeed something to take into account. The main reason I assume that the prices are higher is beacuse the royalties are of 50%, so if the author wants to earn a reasonable amount from their titles (especially for freelancers), the prices has to be higher. So yeah, I can tottally see your side in this, but I also understand why some people would price higher than official products.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T08:51:15-07:00","id":1395605,"title":"","content":"I'm a big Variety kind of man. when Bloodlines: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/281799/Bloodlines-The-Resurrected?term=bloodlines%3A+the+res\" target=\"_blank\">The Resurrected</a> + <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/301087/Bloodlines-The-Devoted\" target=\"_blank\">The Devoted</a> same out on the vault I snatched them up. I love seeing Z-splats and options like that. I'm also a fan of Setting books, the shining hill being <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/271688/Venice-Unmasked\" target=\"_blank\">Venice Unmasked</a>. Basically, anything that gives options and good ideas.<br /> <br /> (Hell, I've built an entire compilation of homebrew templates just from the forums so I can spice up my mortal characters without searching for 5 min (and will one day probably release that doc on the forums with a few of my other projects).).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25117-yackronin","name":"Yackronin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:49:05-07:00","id":1395665,"title":"","content":"Maybe some write ups for courts in Changeling? Like the money one?<br /> <br /> Actually, would promethean sound better? I would like something that has stuff for Extempores","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}